
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="scroll-smooth">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Streamify | Interactive Project Overview</title>
    <!-- Chosen Palette: "Warm Neutral & Muted Violet" - A professional, calm palette with a subtle accent for calls to action, selected to create a modern and clean aesthetic suitable for a technical project presentation. -->
    <!-- Application Structure Plan: The SPA is designed as a thematic, single-page dashboard. This structure replaces the linear reading of the original README with an interactive, explorable experience. Key sections (Features, Demo, Architecture, Setup) are accessible via a sticky navigation bar, allowing users to jump to content relevant to their goals (e.g., a developer going to Setup, a manager viewing Features). This user-centric flow is superior for usability. The highlight is an interactive, non-functional mock-up of the app, providing a tangible feel for the project that text alone cannot. -->
    <!-- Visualization & Content Choices: Report Info -> Goal -> Presentation -> Interaction -> Justification. 1. Features List -> Inform & Organize -> Grid of Cards with Icons -> Hover effects -> More scannable and visually engaging than a plain bulleted list. 2. Project Functionality -> Demonstrate -> Interactive UI Mock-up -> Click stream card to open modal -> Provides a "feel" for the app, making the project's purpose instantly clear. 3. Architectural Decisions -> Explain -> Two-column interactive list -> Click principle to see details -> Breaks down complex info into digestible, user-triggered chunks. 4. Setup Instructions -> Instruct -> Tabbed interface for different modes -> Click tabs to switch content -> Simplifies complex instructions by separating concerns and reducing cognitive load. No charts are used as the source report is purely textual and contains no quantitative data to visualize. -->
    <!-- CONFIRMATION: NO SVG graphics used. NO Mermaid JS used. -->
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-main: #F8F7F4; /* Warm white */
            --bg-secondary: #FFFFFF;
            --surface: #EFECE5;
            --text-primary: #2C2C2C;
            --text-secondary: #585858;
            --accent: #6C5B7B; /* Muted Violet */
            --border-color: #DCD9D1;
        }
        body {
            background-color: var(--bg-main);
            color: var(--text-primary);
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        }
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap');
        .active-nav {
            color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        .active-tab {
             background-color: var(--accent);
             color: white;
        }
        .code-block {
            background-color: #2D2D2D;
            color: #E0E0E0;
            font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
        }
        .section-intro {
             max-width: 700px;
             margin-left: auto;
             margin-right: auto;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="antialiased">

    <!-- Header & Navigation -->
    <header id="header" class="bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-lg sticky top-0 z-50 border-b border-[var(--border-color)]">
        <nav class="container mx-auto px-6 py-4 flex justify-between items-center">
            <a href="#home" class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Streamify Project</a>
            <ul class="hidden md:flex items-center space-x-8 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                <li><a href="#features" class="hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-colors">Features</a></li>
                <li><a href="#demo" class="hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-colors">Live Demo</a></li>
                <li><a href="#architecture" class="hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-colors">Architecture</a></li>
                <li><a href="#setup" class="hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-colors">Setup</a></li>
            </ul>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main>
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <section id="home" class="py-20 md:py-32 bg-[var(--bg-secondary)]">
            <div class="container mx-auto text-center px-6">
                <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--text-primary)]">A Modern Streaming Platform</h2>
                <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-lg text-[var(--text-secondary)]">This is an interactive overview of the Streamify project, a lightweight Twitch-style clone built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to demonstrate core web development proficiency without heavy frameworks.</p>
                <div class="mt-10 flex justify-center gap-4">
                    <a href="#demo" class="bg-[var(--accent)] text-white font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg shadow-md hover:bg-opacity-90 transition-all">View Live Demo</a>
                    <a href="#setup" class="bg-gray-200 text-[var(--text-secondary)] font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 transition-all">Get Started</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Features Section -->
        <section id="features" class="py-20">
            <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
                <div class="text-center mb-12 section-intro">
                    <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold">Project Features</h3>
                    <p class="text-md text-[var(--text-secondary)] mt-2">This section visually breaks down the core functionalities built into the Streamify application. Each card represents a key capability from the source report, designed for quick scanning and comprehension.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
                    <!-- Feature Cards -->
                    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-transparent hover:border-[var(--border-color)] transition-all">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">🎨</div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Responsive Design</h4>
                        <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm">A mobile-first layout that adapts seamlessly to all screen sizes, from phones to desktops.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-transparent hover:border-[var(--border-color)] transition-all">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">🌗</div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Dark/Light Theme</h4>
                        <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm">Supports system preference and manual toggling, with the user's choice saved in `localStorage`.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-transparent hover:border-[var(--border-color)] transition-all">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">🔍</div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Client-Side Search</h4>
                        <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm">A debounced search input to instantly filter streams by title, channel name, or category.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-transparent hover:border-[var(--border-color)] transition-all">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">▶️</div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">HLS Video Playback</h4>
                        <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm">Uses the standard `<video>` element with `hls.js` as a fallback for broad browser compatibility.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-transparent hover:border-[var(--border-color)] transition-all">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">❤️</div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Follow System</h4>
                        <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm">"Follow" and "unfollow" channels, with the state persisted in the browser's `localStorage`.</p>
                    </div>
